# --- Date.now() and new Date(): the host clock, in milliseconds toward negative infinity

=== Date.now at the epoch
@clock 0
Date.now()
--- value
0

=== Date.now drops the nanoseconds
@clock 1704067200123456789
Date.now()
--- value
1704067200123

=== new Date() reads the clock
@clock 1704067200123456789
new Date()
--- value
new Date("2024-01-01T00:00:00.123Z")

=== Date.now a nanosecond before the epoch is -1
@clock -1
[Date.now(), new Date().getTime()]
--- value
[-1,-1]

=== Date.now a millisecond before the epoch
@clock -1000000
[Date.now(), new Date().getTime()]
--- value
[-1,-1]

=== Date.now just before a millisecond before the epoch
@clock -1000001
[Date.now(), new Date().getTime()]
--- value
[-2,-2]

=== Date.now before the epoch, between milliseconds
@clock -1500001
[Date.now(), new Date()]
--- value
[-2,new Date("1969-12-31T23:59:59.998Z")]

=== Date.now at the greatest clock
@clock 8640000000000000000000
[Date.now(), new Date()]
--- value
[8640000000000000,new Date("+275760-09-13T00:00:00.000Z")]

=== Date.now at the least clock
@clock -8640000000000000000000
[Date.now(), new Date()]
--- value
[-8640000000000000,new Date("-271821-04-20T00:00:00.000Z")]

=== Date.now agrees with Temporal.Now
@clock 1704067200999999999
[Date.now() === Temporal.Now.instant().epochMilliseconds, new Date().toISOString(), Temporal.Now.instant()]
--- value
[true,"2024-01-01T00:00:00.999Z",Temporal.Instant.from("2024-01-01T00:00:00.999999999Z")]

=== an Instant of a Date
@clock -86400000000001
Temporal.Instant.fromEpochMilliseconds(new Date().getTime())
--- value
Temporal.Instant.from("1969-12-30T23:59:59.999Z")

=== Date.now without a clock, deliberate
Date.now()
--- fault has not set the clock

=== new Date() without a clock, deliberate
new Date()
--- fault has not set the clock

=== new Date(x) reads no clock
new Date(5).getTime()
--- value
5


