--- fault converts only numbers, booleans, null and undefined


# --- An object, compared by identity, converted by its methods: faults, deliberately

=== === compares identity, deliberate
new Date(0) === new Date(0)
--- fault compares identity

=== - converts with valueOf, deliberate
new Date(5) - new Date(2)
--- fault numbers

=== unary + converts with valueOf, deliberate
+new Date(5)
--- fault numbers

=== < converts with valueOf, deliberate
new Date(1) < new Date(2)
--- fault compares

=== + with a string converts with toString, deliberate
"" + new Date(0)
--- fault adds two numbers

=== a template converts with toString, deliberate
`${new Date(0)}`
--- fault only primitives into strings

=== String converts with toString, deliberate
String(new Date(0))
--- fault only primitives into strings

=== Number converts with valueOf, deliberate
Number(new Date(5))
--- fault converts only

=== a set member, deliberate
new Set([new Date(0)]).size
--- fault primitives only

=== a map key, deliberate
new Map([[new Date(0), 1]]).size
--- fault keys a map by primitives

=== a method read as a value, deliberate
typeof new Date(0).getTime
--- fault does not read them as values

=== Object.keys, deliberate
Object.keys(new Date(0))
--- fault take an object or an array

